Building releases
=================
Following is a table of binaries and their corresponding make invocation. The windows binaries
are preferably built using cross compilation with target x86_64-w64-mingw32. If cross compiling
is not an option, the windows binaries can also be built using an MSYS2 clang64 environment.

See also release.sh.

+------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| Binary                             | Command                                                                                                                              |
+------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| bitbit-x.y-linux-x86-64            | make bitbit-pgo CC=clang ARCH=x86-64-v2 TT=256 STATIC=yes EXE=bitbit-x.y-linux-x86-64                                                |
|                                    |                                                                                                                                      |
| bitbit-x.y-linux-x86-64-avx2       | make bitbit-pgo CC=clang ARCH=x86-64-v3 TT=256 STATIC=yes EXE=bitbit-x.y-linux-x86-64-avx2 SIMD=avx2                                 |
|                                    |                                                                                                                                      |
| bitbit-x.y-windows-x86-64.exe      | make bitbit-pgo CC=clang ARCH=x86-64-v2 TT=256 STATIC=yes EXE=bitbit-x.y-windows-x86-64.exe TARGET=x86_64-w64-mingw32                |
|                                    |                                                                                                                                      |
| bitbit-x.y-windows-x86-64-avx2.exe | make bitbit-pgo CC=clang ARCH=x86-64-v3 TT=256 STATIC=yes EXE=bitbit-x.y-windows-x86-64-avx2.exe SIMD=avx2 TARGET=x86_64-w64-mingw32 |
+------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
